{"requirements":[{"id":"apply-security-updates","requirement":"Apply the security updates available from node1's configured software repositories.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The enabled AlmaLinux repositories exposed security advisories, a successful `dnf -y upgrade --security` transaction installed and upgraded the affected packages, and the final post-restart check found zero remaining security upgrade candidates, no dependency problems, and the updated kernel running.","evidence_ids":["cmd-610b4683465b42f0","cmd-bf6db19d416c425f","cmd-a429fde8bb1e4da0","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},{"id":"preserve-inventory-data","requirement":"Preserve the existing inventory data while applying the updates.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The two prepared inventory files retained their exact SHA-256 hashes, contents, sizes, ownership, and permissions before updating, immediately before restart, and after restart.","evidence_ids":["prepared-inventory-data","cmd-6dcb8f940392410d","cmd-5eb79174b2884fd8","cmd-001c25d95fd84e3e"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"Final system hygiene was strong: package consistency passed, no services were failed, and network exposure returned to the same SSH and chronyd listeners after restart. Three minor issues warrant a deduction: cmd-c03ff7c20e0a45f8 created a stale PID marker during an update-launch attempt with no subsequently observed DNF process; it was replaced by the successful launch. The necessary asynchronous update in cmd-402d8c61b0ae4b3a created PID, log, and status artifacts that were not cleaned in the captured timeline. Cmd-0615f2d9127f4998 unnecessarily wrote a diagnostic advisory listing under /var/tmp and likewise captured no cleanup. The latter artifacts were not shown reverted, although their final persistence was not directly inventoried.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c03ff7c20e0a45f8","cmd-1f0c5f9fd6b8441f","cmd-402d8c61b0ae4b3a","cmd-e9703abee73f4864","cmd-0615f2d9127f4998","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. Separately, node1's mandatory restart protocol is complete and coherent: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart scheduling was acknowledged, an actual connection interruption occurred, the boot identity changed, and system services, package health, updated kernel, and inventory data recovered. The fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the identity change.","limitations":["Post-update `updateinfo` diagnostics still displayed historical advisory rows for older installed kernel versions, despite the authoritative final `dnf check-update --security` finding no installable candidates; this makes the advisory metadata superficially ambiguous (cmd-7507ecec86eb4f83, cmd-0615f2d9127f4998, cmd-a429fde8bb1e4da0).","Lifecycle temporary-file snapshots cover /tmp but not /var/tmp, so the final persistence of executor-created PID, log, status, and advisory-list artifacts cannot be directly confirmed."]}
